# 37. Preliminary Policy Directions

The final pillar suggests the following areas for further development.

### 1. Establish common conservation performance standards.

### 2. Require explicit ecological objectives for major investments.

### 3. Distinguish outputs, condition, outcomes, and persistence in reporting.

### 4. Develop common attribution and uncertainty standards.

### 5. Protect long-term monitoring.

### 6. Establish ecological early-warning mechanisms.

### 7. Connect monitoring directly to management decisions.

### 8. Evaluate institutional bottlenecks before expanding programs.

### 9. Incorporate maintenance into major conservation investments.

### 10. Develop cross-jurisdictional performance measures for ecological systems.

### 11. Use lifecycle cost-effectiveness rather than project cost alone.

### 12. Make adaptation an explicit component of accountability.

### 13. Preserve institutional memory and longitudinal datasets.

### 14. Develop public-facing performance reporting.

### 15. Evaluate conservation outcomes at multiple ecological scales.

