# 38. Research Gaps

Several important questions remain before the final American Conservation Renewal framework can be constructed.

### Measurement

Which ecological indicators are sufficiently standardized for national comparison?

### Attribution

Where is causal evidence strong enough to support investment decisions?

### Data integration

Can existing federal, state, Tribal, and local monitoring systems be linked?

### Institutional accountability

How should responsibility be assigned when ecological outcomes cross jurisdictions?

### Early warning

Which indicators provide sufficient lead time for meaningful intervention?

### Cost-effectiveness

Which interventions produce the largest durable ecological improvements per unit of lifecycle cost?

### Durability

How often do conservation gains persist after active intervention ends?

### Adaptation

Which institutions have demonstrated capacity to change management based on evidence?

### Public reporting

How can performance information be made understandable without oversimplifying ecological uncertainty?

